message.content:
This looks like a CBP ruling on climbing nuts/chocks. Candidate headings are 7616 (other articles of aluminum), 9506 (sports equipment), and 8302 (base metal mountings). I recall that CBP classifies climbing protection devices such as cams and nuts in 9506.99.60 (other articles and equipment for sport), though a few rulings put carabiners in 7616.99.51. Cams are classified in 9506.99.6080 as "other sports equipment." The torque nuts are a composite of an aluminum head, wire and a textile sling, and they are designed specifically for climbing, so 9506 fits.

Within 9506.99, the subheadings are 9506.99.05 (Tennis, etc.), .10 (Fishing?), .15, .20, .25, .30, .35, .40, .45, .55 (Wrist weights?), and .60 (Other). The statistical suffix 9506.99.6080 is "Other." Heading 9506 covers articles for general physical exercise, gymnastics, athletics, other sports, and the aluminum content does not change this. I'll go with 9506.99.6080.

{"hts_code": "9506.99.6080", "reason": "Passive climbing protection devices (aluminum nut heads with wire and textile sling) are specially designed sports equipment classified in heading 9506 as other sports articles and equipment, not as aluminum or base-metal articles."}
